  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nAfter starting synapse, the configured `pid_file` (e.g. `/var/run/matrix-synapse.pid`) is not created.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. start synapse: `su -s /bin/bash -c \"/usr/bin/python3 -m synapse.app.homeserver --config-path /etc/matrix-synapse/homeserver.yaml --config-path /etc/matrix-synapse/conf.d/\" matrix-synapse`\r\n2. look up the location of the configured PID file: `grep -r pid_file /etc/matrix-synapse`\r\n3. verify that the PID file does not exist\r\n\r\nThe documentation of the `pid_file` indicates, that it should be created, when *matrix-synapse* is started as a daemon. Since there is no specific *daemonize* argument, I assume, that this startup mode is the default.\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n1.24.0\r\n\r\n- **Platform**:\r\n\r\nDebian (buster-backports)",
